1
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Experience the dark side of nature

2
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:54,000
Blood Monkey is a action, adventure, horror film directed by Robert Young.

3
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:18,000
Six American grad students have arrived in Africa to
study apes with a renowned professor.

4
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:42,000
But after setting up camp in a jungle clearing, they soon become witness to
the carnage inflicted by the strange and remote species.

5
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:06,000
Professor Hamilton, played by F. Murray Abraham.

6
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:30,000
Seth, played by Matt Ryan.

7
00:30:48,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Amy Armstrong, played by Amy Manson.

8
00:35:12,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Dani Sudeva, played by Freishia Bomanbehram.

9
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:42,000
Greg Satch, played by Matt Reeves.

10
00:44:00,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Chenne, played by Prapimporn Kanjunda.

11
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Blood Monkey is a 2007 American direct-to-video natural horror film
produced by RHI Entertainment and directed by Robert Young.

12
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:54,000
It aired on various video on demand channels, before officially premiering in the United States on
the Syfy Channel (called Sci-Fi channel at the time it premiered) on January 27, 2008.

13
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
Filmed in Thailand, it is the first film in the Maneater film
series produced under an agreement with Syfy.

14
01:01:36,000 --> 01:01:42,000
The film followed a group of six students studying primates in Asia under the demented Professor
Hamilton who find themselves under attack from bloodthirsty primates in the jungle.

15
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
Reviewers panned the film, criticizing the acting, dialogue, plot, low-quality special
effects, and the lack of appearances by the titular monster, the monkeys.

16
01:10:24,000 --> 01:10:30,000
They also questioned the appearance of F.

17
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:54,000
Murray Abraham in the film, though note that his
performance was its only positive aspect.

18
01:19:12,000 --> 01:19:18,000
The film explores themes of expedition, mad scientist, jungle, killer ape.

19
01:23:36,000 --> 01:23:42,000
The tone is dark.
